WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.567 --> 00:00:02.202
-Whoo!

00:00:02.202 --> 00:00:03.603
You can sit down.
Sit down.

00:00:03.603 --> 00:00:04.804
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:04.804 --> 00:00:07.173
Sit down!

00:00:07.173 --> 00:00:09.843
It is actually my 50th birthday.

00:00:09.843 --> 00:00:11.811
Yeah!

00:00:11.811 --> 00:00:13.112
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.112 --> 00:00:14.714
Yes.

00:00:14.714 --> 00:00:18.551
I've had two very humbling
experiences in the last year.

00:00:18.551 --> 00:00:19.986
I almost had to get a job.

00:00:19.986 --> 00:00:21.321
Whew!

00:00:21.321 --> 00:00:23.789
I got close.

00:00:23.789 --> 00:00:25.457
I had an interview,
and the woman noticed --

00:00:25.457 --> 00:00:27.494
I haven't had a job since 2010.

00:00:27.494 --> 00:00:28.794
And the lady interviewing me,
she's like,

00:00:28.794 --> 00:00:32.198
"I see you haven't had
a corporate job since 2010.

00:00:32.198 --> 00:00:33.699
What have been you doing?"

00:00:33.699 --> 00:00:35.935
I learned the wrong answer is,
"The best I can."

00:00:35.935 --> 00:00:37.236
[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.236 --> 00:00:39.406
They don't like that.
[ Laughs ]

00:00:39.406 --> 00:00:41.374
'Cause at my age,
I like job interviews.

00:00:41.374 --> 00:00:42.274
They're fun.

00:00:42.274 --> 00:00:43.909
I tell the truth now.

00:00:43.909 --> 00:00:45.211
They all ask the same question.

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:47.313
They're like, "Jackie,
what are your weaknesses?

00:00:47.313 --> 00:00:48.681
What should you work at
harder in life?

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:49.582
What are you weak at?"

00:00:49.582 --> 00:00:51.484
And I'm, like, "Uh, working."

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:52.418
[ Laughter ]

00:00:52.418 --> 00:00:53.452
"I can't hold a job.

00:00:53.452 --> 00:00:55.654
Duh, that's why I'm here."

00:00:55.654 --> 00:00:57.456
[ Laughs ]

00:00:57.456 --> 00:00:59.658
Next question, "Jackie,
what are you good at?

00:00:59.658 --> 00:01:01.127
What are your assets?"

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:03.328
I said, "Sir, I can work eight
hours a day, five days a week,

00:01:03.328 --> 00:01:04.430
and not do a damn thing."

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:05.464
Anybody else?

00:01:05.464 --> 00:01:07.066
So good.

00:01:07.066 --> 00:01:09.669
Favorite one --
"What are your five year goals?

00:01:09.669 --> 00:01:11.570
Where do you see yourself
in five years?"

00:01:11.570 --> 00:01:13.439
I'm like, "Hopefully having
an affair with the VP

00:01:13.439 --> 00:01:14.641
so I ain't got to work no more."

00:01:14.641 --> 00:01:16.209
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.209 --> 00:01:17.376
Didn't work.

00:01:17.376 --> 00:01:19.846
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:21.014 --> 00:01:23.149
[ Sighs ]

00:01:23.149 --> 00:01:24.350
Every job I've had,

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:25.785
I've always been
the only Black girl,

00:01:25.785 --> 00:01:26.986
surrounded by white people.

00:01:26.986 --> 00:01:28.487
And I always had to be
three different women,

00:01:28.487 --> 00:01:29.789
every job.

00:01:29.789 --> 00:01:32.558
I'm Jackie for you guys.
My family calls me Jacqueline.

00:01:32.558 --> 00:01:33.993
I'm also Jaqueesha,

00:01:33.993 --> 00:01:37.296
the Black girl from the Bronx
who comes out at the wrong time.

00:01:37.296 --> 00:01:39.432
I was at a corporate job once,
and they had Secret Santa.

00:01:39.432 --> 00:01:41.734
What's a normal amount?
$10?

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:44.203
They raised it one year to $50.

00:01:44.203 --> 00:01:45.538
Jaqueesha jumped out.

00:01:45.538 --> 00:01:47.440
I was like, "I wish I would
give up $50.

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:48.808
Diane is a whore.

00:01:48.808 --> 00:01:50.376
I hate this company.

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:51.711
Oh, my God.
Was that Jaqueesha?

00:01:51.711 --> 00:01:52.946
How'd she get here?"

00:01:52.946 --> 00:01:54.146
[ Applause ]

00:01:54.146 --> 00:01:55.648
[ Laughs ]

00:01:55.648 --> 00:01:57.283
My bad.

00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:58.417
Jaqueesha been to jail.

00:01:58.417 --> 00:01:59.552
I'm sorry.
I didn't know.

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:01.788
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.788 --> 00:02:03.322
My next humbling experience,

00:02:03.322 --> 00:02:06.993
I had to move back home
with my retired Jamaican mother.

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:08.661
Yeah.

00:02:08.661 --> 00:02:10.830
And I have learned
that she is a liar.

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:12.031
Okay?

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:13.299
Everyone's worried about her.

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:14.934
They're like, "Miss Carol,
are you staying home?

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:16.435
Are you being nice and safe?"

00:02:16.435 --> 00:02:18.804
She's like, "Baby girl,
I'm so scared of the COVID,

00:02:18.804 --> 00:02:20.172
I don't leave the house."

00:02:20.172 --> 00:02:21.174
The woman is a liar.

00:02:21.174 --> 00:02:22.876
She's gone every day
for three hours.

00:02:22.876 --> 00:02:24.176
I don't know where she goes.

00:02:24.176 --> 00:02:27.013
She comes back with two bananas,
an apple, a mango.

00:02:27.013 --> 00:02:28.948
This is not essential.
What's going on with you?

00:02:28.948 --> 00:02:31.517
[ Laughter ]

00:02:31.517 --> 00:02:34.520
I accidentally got in
a really serious relationship

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:35.955
when the pandemic started.

00:02:35.955 --> 00:02:37.957
Yeah. 'Cause they were like,
"You can't date."

00:02:37.957 --> 00:02:39.392
And I'm not going to be alone
for a year.

00:02:39.392 --> 00:02:40.693
Somebody love me!

00:02:40.693 --> 00:02:43.029
So I found someone
who I've known for a long time.

00:02:43.029 --> 00:02:45.230
I told him so many lies

00:02:45.230 --> 00:02:48.367
to make him think I'm
the quarantine wife you want.

00:02:48.367 --> 00:02:50.870
I said, "Look,
I'm a domestic Goddess.

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:53.172
I cook all my meals
from scratch.

00:02:53.172 --> 00:02:54.774
I even grow my own vegetables."

00:02:54.774 --> 00:02:56.208
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:56.208 --> 00:02:58.945
Somehow, I found a man who
actually does cook and garden.

00:02:58.945 --> 00:03:00.146
He had a whole thing prepared.

00:03:00.146 --> 00:03:01.914
He was like, "You and I
should garden together."

00:03:01.914 --> 00:03:03.949
He had two packs of greens
that had the roots,

00:03:03.949 --> 00:03:05.518
and told me -- Hey! --

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:06.786
and told me, "Take one home."

00:03:06.786 --> 00:03:07.787
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.787 --> 00:03:09.021
Ha-ha!

00:03:09.021 --> 00:03:11.623
Told me to take one --
He said, "take one home

00:03:11.623 --> 00:03:13.559
and plant yours;
I'll plant mine.

00:03:13.559 --> 00:03:15.995
And we can watch them
grow together as a couple."

00:03:15.995 --> 00:03:18.297
[ Audience "Awws" ]
I was, like, "Oh, my God!

00:03:18.297 --> 00:03:19.532
Garden.
I lied to you.

00:03:19.532 --> 00:03:21.233
I'd rather die.
Look at these nails!"

00:03:21.233 --> 00:03:23.736
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:23.736 --> 00:03:25.138
"Okay?"

00:03:28.374 --> 00:03:29.642
I barely have the strength

00:03:29.642 --> 00:03:31.811
to take a shower on Fridays
during the pandemic.

00:03:31.811 --> 00:03:33.413
I'm not gonna plant asparagus.

00:03:33.413 --> 00:03:34.713
[ Laughter ]

00:03:34.713 --> 00:03:36.616
'Cause he wants us to be
Martha Stewart and Snoop Dogg.

00:03:36.616 --> 00:03:38.217
Guess what?
He's Martha. I'm Snoop.

00:03:38.217 --> 00:03:39.618
I don't do any of that.

00:03:39.618 --> 00:03:41.053
That was a lie.

00:03:41.053 --> 00:03:42.621
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:42.621 --> 00:03:45.124
Now it's time to tackle
some of my pandy weight.

00:03:45.124 --> 00:03:47.226
Panoramic weight.
Little chunky monkey.

00:03:47.226 --> 00:03:49.595
I was before, but now
it's really a problem.

00:03:49.595 --> 00:03:51.430
Nobody should be sadder
when this is over more

00:03:51.430 --> 00:03:52.598
than white women.

00:03:52.598 --> 00:03:55.201
The way you women started
baking like convicts

00:03:55.201 --> 00:03:56.202
on TikTok...

00:03:56.202 --> 00:03:57.704
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.704 --> 00:03:59.872
Okay, the zucchini bread,
the banana bread,

00:03:59.872 --> 00:04:01.307
the bananas you saved,

00:04:01.307 --> 00:04:03.109
the sourdough
the size of my head.

00:04:03.109 --> 00:04:06.346
Why? And then I'm following
Stacy's recipes on TikTok,

00:04:06.346 --> 00:04:07.446
and she ain't gaining no weight.

00:04:07.446 --> 00:04:08.714
Go to hell, Stacy.

00:04:08.714 --> 00:04:10.350
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:11.550
Okay?

00:04:11.550 --> 00:04:13.453
I grew a third breast
during this pandemic.

00:04:13.453 --> 00:04:14.920
[ Laughter ]

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:18.191
And it's made of sourdough,
okay?

00:04:18.191 --> 00:04:19.792
With all of my humbling,
you know,

00:04:19.792 --> 00:04:21.427
I had one thing
that's really humbling --

00:04:21.427 --> 00:04:24.997
I'm living in the same childhood
bedroom that I grew up in.

00:04:24.997 --> 00:04:26.833
Yeah, same room.

00:04:26.833 --> 00:04:29.768
The first orgasm I ever had
in my entire life

00:04:29.768 --> 00:04:30.903
was in this bedroom.

00:04:30.903 --> 00:04:32.204
And that was alone then, too.

00:04:32.204 --> 00:04:33.906
So life is full circle.

00:04:33.906 --> 00:04:35.641
Stay humble.
Remember where you come from.

00:04:35.641 --> 00:04:37.744
I'm Jackie Fabulous, guys.
Thank you so much.

